  "items": [
   {
    "id": "ex-cg-s4-coset-minima-and-double-coset-decomposition",
    "kind": "example",
    "title": "Left and right coset minima and a double coset decomposition in S4",
    "deps": [
     "def-cg-parabolic-quotient-and-two-sided-minima",
     "thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization",
     "thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form",
     "lem-cg-double-coset-intersection-parabolic",
     "def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length",
     "thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity"
    ],
    "statement": "Let $W=S_4$ with simple reflections $s_1=(1\\,2)$, $s_2=(2\\,3)$, $s_3=(3\\,4)$, so that $m(s_i,s_j)=3$ if $|i-j|=1$ and $=2$ if $|i-j|=2$ ([[def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length]]). Write permutations in one-line notation, so that $s_1=2134$, $s_2=1324$, $s_3=1243$, and $\\ell(w)$ is the inversion number ([[thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity]] (4)). Fix $I=\\{s_1,s_2\\}$, $J=\\{s_2,s_3\\}$ and, for $K\\subseteq I$, let $W_I^K=\\{u\\in W_I:\\ell(us)>\\ell(u)\\ \\text{for all }s\\in K\\}$.\n\n**(i) The parabolics.** $W_I=\\{w:w(4)=4\\}=\\{1234,1324,2134,2314,3124,3214\\}$ and $W_J=\\{w:w(1)=1\\}=\\{1234,1243,1324,1342,1423,1432\\}$, both of order $6$, and $W_I\\cap W_J=W_{I\\cap J}=W_{\\{s_2\\}}=\\{1234,1324\\}$ ([[thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization]] (1)).\n\n**(ii) The quotients.** $W^J=\\{w:\\ell(ws_i)>\\ell(w)\\ (i=2,3)\\}=\\{1234,2134,3124,4123\\}$, ${}^IW=\\{w:\\ell(s_iw)>\\ell(w)\\ (i=1,2)\\}=\\{1234,1243,1423,4123\\}$, and ${}^IW^J=\\{1234,4123\\}$; hence $S_4$ is the disjoint union of exactly two double cosets $W_IwW_J$ ([[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (1)).\n\n**(iii) The two double cosets.** The double coset $W_I\\,1234\\,W_J$ has $18$ elements, minimum $d=1234$ (length $0$) and $K=\\{s_2\\}$ with $W_I^K=\\{1234,2134,3124\\}$; the double coset $W_I\\,4123\\,W_J$ has $6$ elements, minimum $d=4123$ (length $3$) and $K=\\{s_1,s_2\\}$ with $W_I^K=\\{1234\\}$. In both cases $|W_IwW_J|=|W_I^K|\\cdot|W_J|$, and $18=6\\cdot6/2$, $6=6\\cdot6/6$ in agreement with [[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (2),(3).\n\n**(iv) Coset minima and a normal form of a single element.** For $w=2143$ (so $\\ell(w)=2$): the element of minimum length in $W_Iw$ is $1243$ (of length $1$), the element of minimum length in $wW_J$ is $2134$ (of length $1$), and the double coset $W_IwW_J$ has minimum $d=1234$ and normal form\n$$2143=2134\\cdot 1234\\cdot 1243,\\qquad \\ell(2134)+\\ell(1234)+\\ell(1243)=1+0+1=2=\\ell(2143),$$\nwith $2134\\in W_I^K$ for $K=\\{s_2\\}$ and $1243\\in W_J$ ([[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (2)).\n\n**(v) A second pair of parabolics.** For $I=\\{s_1\\}$ and $J=\\{s_3\\}$ one has ${}^IW^J=\\{1234,1324,1423,3124,3412,4123,4312\\}$ ($7$ elements), the seven double cosets have sizes $4,4,4,4,4,2,2$ and minima $1234,1324,1423,3124,4123,3412,4312$ respectively, and the associated sets are $K=\\emptyset$ for the first five minima and $K=\\{s_1\\}$ for $d=3412$ and $d=4312$ (so $W_I^K=\\{1,s_1\\}$ or $W_I^K=\\{1\\}$ respectively); for instance\n$$W_I\\,3412\\,W_J=\\{3412,3421\\},\\qquad W_I\\,4123\\,W_J=\\{4123,4132,4213,4231\\}.$$\nThis exhibits a case where $K$ varies with $d$ and $|W_IwW_J|$ is not constant.",
    "strategy": "All assertions are finite computations in the group $S_4$ of order $24$, with $W_I$, $W^J$, ${}^IW$, ${}^IW^J$ and $W_I^K$ as in [[def-cg-parabolic-quotient-and-two-sided-minima]], using the identification $\\ell=$ inversion number from [[thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity]] (4) and the description of $W_I$, $W_J$ by fixed points from part (1) of the same theorem.\n**(i)** Direct listing: $W_I$ consists of the permutations with $w(4)=4$ and $W_J$ of those with $w(1)=1$; their intersection consists of $1234$ and $1324=s_2$, which is $W_{I\\cap J}$ by [[thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization]] (1).\n**(ii),(iii)** One computes the descent sets directly: $w\\in W^J$ iff $w(2)<w(3)$ and $w(3)<w(4)$, and $w\\in{}^IW$ iff $w(1)<w(2)$ and $w(2)<w(3)$; this gives the four-element sets displayed, whose intersection is $\\{1234,4123\\}$. The double coset of $1234$ is $\\{udv:u\\in W_I,v\\in W_J\\}$ and one checks by listing that it has $18$ elements, while the complement (the double coset of $4123$) has the remaining $6$. For $d=1234$ and $d=4123$ the set $K=\\{s\\in I:d^{-1}sd\\in J\\}$ is $\\{s_2\\}$ respectively $\\{s_1,s_2\\}$, computed by conjugating $s_1,s_2$ by $d^{-1}$; the sets $W_I^K$ are then found by the right-descent tests $\\ell(us_2)>\\ell(u)$, and the multiplicativity of sizes is a direct count, checked against [[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (3).\n**(iv)** The cosets are $W_Iw=\\{1243,1342,2143,2341,3142,3241\\}$ and $wW_J=\\{2134,2143,2314,2341,2413,2431\\}$; their minima are read off from the lists, and $2143=2134\\cdot1234\\cdot1243$ is the unique factorization of [[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (2) with $u=2134=s_1\\in W_I^K$ and $v=1243=s_3\\in W_J$.\n**(v)** For $I=\\{s_1\\}$, $J=\\{s_3\\}$ the double cosets are the orbits of the group generated by left $s_1$ and right $s_3$ multiplications; listing the $24$ elements gives the seven minima and sizes as displayed, and $K=\\emptyset$ or $\\{s_1\\}$ according to whether $d^{-1}s_1d\\in\\{s_3\\}$; the two displayed double cosets are computed directly. In particular $K$ is not a function of the pair $(I,J)$ alone, which is why it must be recomputed for each $d$ as in [[lem-cg-double-coset-intersection-parabolic]]. No use of the Axiom of Choice is made.",
    "sources": {
     "references": [
      {
       "title": "Anders Bjorner and Francesco Brenti, Combinatorics of Coxeter Groups (Graduate Texts in Mathematics 231, Springer 2005; author-hosted complete PDF)",
       "url": "https://sites.math.washington.edu/~billey/classes/reflection.groups/references/EntireBook.pdf",
       "locator": "Section 2.4, printed pp. 38-45 (Proposition 2.4.4, Corollary 2.4.5 and the Young-subgroup description of parabolic subgroups of S_n) and Exercise 15, printed p. 58."
      },
      {
       "title": "Sara Billey, Matjaz Konvalinka, T. Kyle Petersen, William Slofstra and Bridget Tenner, Parabolic double cosets in Coxeter groups (arXiv:1612.00736v2)",
       "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.00736v2",
       "locator": "Section 2.2, printed pp. 7-8 of the arXiv version (Proposition 2.7 and Corollary 2.8, the double coset formula |W_IwW_J|=|W_I||W_J|/|W_H| for finite parabolics), and Section 3 for the S_n setting."
      },
      {
       "title": "George Lusztig, Hecke Algebras with Unequal Parameters (revised arXiv edition of the CRM monograph, arXiv:math/0208154v2)",
       "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0208154v2",
       "locator": "Chapter 9, Proposition 9.15(a)-(d) (printed pp. 44-45), whose statements are instantiated by the computations above."
      }
     ]
    },
    "provenance": {
