   },
   {
    "id": "ex-cg-infinite-dihedral-parabolic-double-cosets",
    "kind": "example",
    "title": "Parabolic double cosets of the infinite dihedral group",
    "deps": [
     "def-cg-parabolic-quotient-and-two-sided-minima",
     "thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization",
     "thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form",
     "def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length",
     "lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign",
     "thm-cg-root-length-criterion-and-faithfulness",
     "def-cg-canonical-reflection-homomorphism",
     "def-group-homomorphism",
     "thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity"
    ],
    "statement": "Let $S=\\{s,t\\}$ with $m(s,t)=\\infty$, so that $W=\\langle s,t\\rangle$ is the infinite dihedral group with length $\\ell$ ([[def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length]]); put $u:=st$, so that $u$ has infinite order, $W=\\{u^k:k\\in\\mathbb Z\\}\\cup\\{u^ks:k\\in\\mathbb Z\\}$, $sus^{-1}=u^{-1}$, and $\\ell(u^k)=2|k|$ for every $k$, while $\\ell(u^ks)=2|k|+1$ for $k\\ge0$ and $\\ell(u^ks)=2|k|-1$ for $k\\le-1$ ([[lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign]] (3)(c), (4) and (7): the alternating words representing these elements are reduced). Let $I=\\{s\\}$ and $J=\\{t\\}$, so that $W_I=\\{1,s\\}$, $W_J=\\{1,t\\}$ and $W_I\\cap W_J=W_\\emptyset=\\{1\\}$ ([[thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization]] (1)); these are the *standard* parabolics of rank $1$.\n\n**(i) All parabolics of $W$.** The parabolic subgroups of $W$ are exactly $\\{1\\}$, the order-two subgroups $\\{1,r\\}$ generated by a reflection $r\\in T$, and $W$; in particular $W_I$ and $W_J$ are distinct conjugate-free standard parabolics with trivial intersection.\n\n**(ii) The quotients.** ${}^IW=\\{w:\\ell(sw)>\\ell(w)\\}=\\{u^{-k}:k\\ge0\\}\\cup\\{u^{-k}s:k\\ge1\\}=\\{1,t,ts,tst,\\dots\\}$, $W^J=\\{w:\\ell(wt)>\\ell(w)\\}=\\{u^{k}:k\\le0\\}\\cup\\{u^ks:k\\ge0\\}=\\{1,s,sts,ts,tsts,\\dots\\}$, and ${}^IW^J=(ts)^{\\mathbb N}=\\{1,ts,tsts,tststs,\\dots\\}=\\{u^{-k}:k\\ge0\\}$: the two-sided descent-free elements are exactly the powers of the translation $ts$.\n\n**(iii) The double cosets.** For every $k\\ge0$ the set $W_I(ts)^kW_J$ is a double coset with exactly four elements,\n$$W_I(ts)^kW_J=\\{(ts)^k,\\ s(ts)^k,\\ (ts)^kt,\\ s(ts)^kt\\}=\\{u^{-k},\\ u^{k}s,\\ u^{-(k+1)}s,\\ u^{k+1}\\},$$\nof lengths $2k,2k+1,2k+1,2k+2$, and its minimum is $d_k=(ts)^k$ with length $2k$ ([[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (2)). Here $K=\\{s'\\in I:d_k^{-1}s'd_k\\in J\\}$ is empty for every $k\\ge0$, so $W_I^K=W_I$, and $|W_I(ts)^kW_J|=4=|W_I|\\cdot|W_J|/|W_K|$ in agreement with (3) of the same theorem. Finally $W$ is the disjoint union of the double cosets $W_I(ts)^kW_J$, $k\\ge0$; the first one is\n$$W_IW_J=\\{1,s,t,st\\},$$\nand as $k$ runs over $\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}$ the elements $u^{-k},u^ks,u^{-(k+1)}s,u^{k+1}$ of these blocks exhaust the lists $u^m$ and $u^ms$ ($m\\in\\mathbb Z$) without repetition, so the decomposition is exhaustive and the parts are disjoint.",
    "strategy": "**(i)** By [[def-cg-parabolic-quotient-and-two-sided-minima]] (4) the parabolic subgroups are the conjugates of $W_I$ for $I\\subseteq S$; here the subsets are $\\emptyset,\\{s\\},\\{t\\},\\{s,t\\}$, giving $\\{1\\}$, $\\{1,s\\}$, $\\{1,t\\}$ and $W$, and the conjugates of $\\{1,s\\}$ and $\\{1,t\\}$ in $W$ are exactly the subgroups $\\{1,r\\}$ with $r\\in T$ ([[def-cg-canonical-reflection-homomorphism]]). Since $T$ contains elements other than $s,t$ (for example $tst$, which is $\\rho$-conjugate to $s$), these are the conjugates of the standard ones; no other parabolic subgroups occur.\n**(ii)** By the criterion $\\ell(sw)>\\ell(w)\\Leftrightarrow \\rho(w)^{-1}e_s\\in\\Phi_+$ of [[thm-cg-root-length-criterion-and-faithfulness]] (1) applied to $d^{-1}$ — or directly from the reduced expressions — the elements with no left descent at $s$ are exactly those whose reduced expression is $1$ or starts with $t$, i.e. $\\{u^{-k}:k\\ge0\\}\\cup\\{u^{-k}s:k\\ge1\\}$, and the elements with no right descent at $t$ are $1$ or those whose reduced expression ends in $s$, i.e. $\\{u^k:k\\le0\\}\\cup\\{u^ks:k\\ge0\\}$; intersecting gives the powers $u^{-k}=(ts)^k$. The displayed initial terms follow from $u^{-1}=ts$, $u^{-1}s=t$, $u^{-2}s=tst$.\n**(iii)** By [[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] every double coset has the form $W_I d_k W_J$ with $d_k\\in{}^IW^J$, so $d_k=(ts)^k$ for some $k\\ge0$; multiplying the four elements $u\\in W_I$, $v\\in W_J$ into $d_k$ gives the four displayed elements, which are pairwise distinct by the normal form $W=\\{u^m\\}\\cup\\{u^ms\\}$ with distinct $m$ ([[lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign]] (4)); their lengths are read off from the reduced alternating expressions: $\\ell(u^m)=2|m|$ for all $m$, $\\ell(u^ms)=2|m|+1$ for $m\\ge0$, and $\\ell(u^{-(k+1)}s)=2k+1$. The set $K$ is computed from $d_k^{-1}sd_k=u^ksu^{-k}$, which is a reflection about $2k$ (the reflection $u^ksu^{-k}=\\rho(d_k)^{-1}s\\rho(d_k)$, to be read in the presentation of [[lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign]]), and this is not $t$ for any $k\\ge0$; hence $K=\\emptyset$. The count $4=2\\cdot2/1$ is the finite-case formula of [[thm-cg-double-coset-unique-minimum-and-normal-form]] (3). Exhaustiveness and disjointness follow because every element of $W$ is some $u^m$ or $u^ms$ with $m\\in\\mathbb Z$ unique, and the blocks $W_I(ts)^kW_J=\\{u^{-k},u^ks,u^{-(k+1)}s,u^{k+1}\\}$, $k\\ge0$, sort exactly these elements without repetition. No use of the Axiom of Choice is made.",
    "sources": {
     "references": [
      {
